{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Even</b> — the meaning, if you read it as heavenly decrees that HaShem decreed from days of old for evil to come into the world, and the evil is likened to גיא צלמות (a valley of deep darkness): I will fear no evil — I will not fear that evil will befall me, for Your staff shows me the way until I depart, and this is the staff and the support by which one's heart is comforted. And the meaning: when a year of evil comes upon the world, HaShem brings about causes for those who take refuge in Him, to keep them alive in famine and to deliver their lives from death. And the meaning of מות is death not in the natural course, like the dead of war and plague."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:23.089077759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}